  "source_scope_note": "The selected problem is Theorem 7.1 for transverse intersections with no common vertices of balanced geodesic graphs, on a closed connected oriented hyperbolic surface of genus at least two. The complete author article body retains all local graph-cocycle, adjoint flat-bundle closed-form, vertex extension and weighted Killing-form/Stokes computation. Eleven original graphical illustrations are retained as figure-only source assets; all captions, proof prose and formulas remain editable. Nontransverse isotopy extensions, geometric motivation and universal-surjectivity claims are unselected context.",
